WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
Two phones.

2
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.750
The same one-word reply on each: sure.

3
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.290
Except one of them has a full stop.

4
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.540
Two readers look at their screens.

5
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.100
Would they feel the same?

6
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.350
Can one tiny dot change a whole message?

7
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.300
Is a full stop in a text message rude?

8
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:22.610
In this mission, you'll see how text messages
mix the features of speech and writing.

9
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.290
You'll explore emoji, initialisms, and
other tricks that stand in for a voice

10
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.500
and a face.

11
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.600
And you'll look at how researchers tested
what readers really make of that dot.

12
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.800
Your mission: decide whether
a full stop in a text is rude.
